# Wine: share relocated pages of the shared section copies (on top of 0001).
#
# 0001 shares one page-aligned copy of chrome.dll's big read-only sections, but chrome.dll is
# mapped at the server-assigned dynamic base, not its preferred one, and every process then
# relocated the copy privately: ~18 MB of dirty, unshared pages per process (x ~40 at startup).
# wineserver assigns one map address per file, so it can pre-relocate the copy for that address
# (as the Windows kernel shares relocated image pages); the client skips those blocks when it
# really sits at that address, and otherwise falls back to private copies. Per-renderer dirty
# shared-copy pages 18.2 MB -> 40 KB; startup peak (no KSM) ~1500 -> ~1150 MB.
# The pe_image_info bit comes out of the existing padding; same struct size.
# Ours, not upstream. LGPL-2.1-or-later.
